---
// src/pages/index.astro
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Downloader from "../components/Downloader.astro";
import Features from "../components/Features.astro";
import HowToUse from "../components/HowToUse.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Free Bulk Image Downloader Online - Download from URL List"
  description="Need a bulk image downloader from URL list or webpage? Try the best free bulk image downloader online. Fast, secure client-side batch downloader."
>
  <!-- Hero Section with Decorative Atmospheric Mesh Gradient -->
  <section
    class="relative overflow-hidden pt-12 pb-20 border-b border-hairline bg-canvas rounded-lg mb-12"
  >
    <!-- Mesh Gradient Backdrop -->
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 -top-40 -left-40 h-[600px] w-[800px] mesh-gradient pointer-events-none"
    >
    </div>
    <div
      class="absolute right-0 top-0 h-[500px] w-[500px] mesh-gradient pointer-events-none"
      style="opacity: 0.08;"
    >
    </div>

    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center px-4">
      <span
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-link-bg-soft px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-link mb-6"
      >
        ⚡ 100% Client-Side & Secure
      </span>
      <h1
        class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-6 font-sans"
      >
        Download images in bulk, instantly.
      </h1>
      <p
        class="text-lg md:text-xl text-body mb-8 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto"
      >
        Paste a list of image URLs or extract images from any webpage. Package
        them instantly into a single ZIP file without exhausting your server
        bandwidth or compromising privacy.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="#downloader"
          class="rounded-pill bg-primary px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-on-primary hover:bg-neutral-800 transition-colors shadow-sm"
        >
          Start Downloading
        </a>
        <a
          href="#features"
          class="rounded-pill border border-hairline bg-canvas px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-body hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 transition-colors"
        >
          Learn More
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Reusable Downloader Component (Direct tab active by default) -->
  <Downloader defaultTab="direct" />

  <!-- Reusable Features Grid Component -->
  <Features />

  <!-- Reusable How To Use Guide Component -->
  <HowToUse />

  <!-- Comprehensive SEO Guide Section (800 - 1200 words) -->
  <section
    id="seo-guide"
    class="max-w-[1000px] mx-auto border-t border-hairline pt-20 mb-20 scroll-mt-20"
  >
    <div class="bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-lg p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-12 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-6 font-sans border-b border-hairline pb-4">
        The Ultimate Guide to Free Bulk Image Downloader Online
      </h2>
      
      <div class="prose max-w-none text-sm text-body leading-relaxed space-y-6">
        <p>
          In today's digital landscape, content creators, developers, designers, and marketers deal with thousands of images daily. Manually downloading images one by one is tedious, time-consuming, and highly inefficient. That is why a high-performance <strong>free bulk image downloader</strong> is an essential utility.
        </p>
        
        <p>
          Whether you need to extract media assets for a website migration, download mockups for a client presentation, or compile research datasets, having the right tool makes all the difference. Our <strong>free bulk image downloader online</strong> is engineered to simplify this workflow. By allowing you to extract images directly from a <strong>bulk image downloader from url list</strong> or crawl any live webpage, this application offers unmatched convenience—completely free, private, and running entirely in your browser.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-8 mb-4 font-sans">
          Why Choose a Web-Based Bulk Image Downloader Free Tool?
        </h3>
        
        <p>
          Many users default to searching for a <strong>download bulk image downloader</strong> software installer or searching for browser extensions. However, web-based utilities offer major advantages:
        </p>
        
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Zero Installation</strong>: With a <strong>bulk image downloader online</strong>, you do not need to download executables that might contain malware or bloat your operating system.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Platform Independence</strong>: It runs anywhere there is a modern browser—whether you are on Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS, or mobile.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>100% Secure & Private</strong>: Unlike typical server-side tools, our <strong>bulk image downloader free</strong> application processes files locally in your browser. Your source URL list and downloaded image blobs are never uploaded to our servers, keeping your data confidential.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-8 mb-4 font-sans">
          Crawl and Extract: Bulk Image Downloader from URL List
        </h3>
        
        <p>
          The most common workflow for automation is downloading a pre-compiled list of links. Our utility is the perfect <strong>free bulk image downloader from url list</strong>. 
        </p>
        
        <p>
          If you have a CSV, a spreadsheet column, or a text document containing image links, you can paste the entire block directly into our input workspace. The engine automatically handles parsing, filters out duplicate links, cleans up whitespace, and queues them for downloading. 
        </p>
        
        <p>
          With support for all major image formats—including WebP, PNG, JPG, JPEG, GIF, SVG, AVIF, and ICO formats—you can rest assured that your target file extensions are fully supported. Once the links are processed, the <strong>best bulk image downloader</strong> engine downloads them simultaneously, bundles them into a structured ZIP file, and lets you download the package in a single click.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-8 mb-4 font-sans">
          Webpage Extraction vs. Chrome Bulk Image Downloader
        </h3>
        
        <p>
          Many professionals search for a <strong>chrome bulk image downloader</strong> or a <strong>bulk image downloader chrome</strong> extension. While browser extensions are useful, they come with significant permission warnings and security risks, as they can read all data on the websites you visit.
        </p>
        
        <p>
          Our online extractor functions as a powerful alternative. By pasting a single URL, you activate our extraction engine which automatically crawls the page. It extracts classic <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> tags and their responsive <code>srcset</code> variations, inline CSS background styles (e.g. <code>background-image: url(...)</code>), and anchor links <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> pointing directly to image files. This gives you all the scraping power of a <strong>chrome bulk image downloader</strong> without compromising your browser's security or exposing your private browsing data.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-8 mb-4 font-sans">
          Core Features of the Best Bulk Image Downloader
        </h3>
        
        <p>
          To ensure we built the <strong>best bulk image downloader</strong> on the web, we addressed the biggest pain points of competitor sites like bulkimagedownloader.in:
        </p>
        
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Local Browser Packaging</strong>: Instead of dragging your bandwidth down by downloading files individually, our client-side Javascript engine bundles everything into a single <code>.zip</code> file on your system.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Granular Extension Filters</strong>: Only need SVG icons? Or maybe just high-resolution WebP images? Switch between file format tabs to filter and select exactly what you need.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>CORS Proxy Fallback</strong>: Browsers block direct image downloads from external domains due to Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) security rules. Our engine automatically detects these blocks and channels the request through a secure proxy to guarantee a 100% download success rate.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Live Previews & Resolution Stats</strong>: View thumbnails, file formats, and estimated file sizes in real time before triggering your final download.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-8 mb-4 font-sans">
          How to Use the Free Bulk Image Downloader Online
        </h3>
        
        <p>
          Getting started is simple. Follow these steps to batch-download your assets:
        </p>
        
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Select Mode</strong>: Choose between <strong>Paste URL List</strong> or <strong>Extract From Webpage</strong> tabs.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Input Targets</strong>: Paste your list of image URLs (one per line) or enter the single webpage URL you wish to scrape.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Analyze</strong>: Click the action button to let our parser process the links.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Filter & Select</strong>: Use the visual grid to preview the images. You can deselect thumbnails you don’t want (such as tiny tracking icons) or filter by file extension.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Download</strong>: Enter a custom name for your package and click "Download Selected". Your browser will automatically trigger the ZIP file download once processing completes.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 border-t border-hairline pt-8">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-6 font-sans">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h3>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
            <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink mb-2">
              Is this bulk image downloader free to use?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Yes, this is a 100% <strong>bulk image downloader free</strong> utility. There are no registration forms, no usage limits, and no premium tiers. You can download as many images as you need, whenever you need them.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
            <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink mb-2">
              How does it compare to a chrome bulk image downloader extension?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Unlike a <strong>bulk image downloader chrome</strong> extension, our tool is web-based and does not require installation. This keeps your browser clean and safe from extensions that scan your web history.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
            <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink mb-2">
              Can I run a bulk image downloader from url list offline?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              While you need an active internet connection to retrieve external images, all image parsing and ZIP packaging tasks are performed locally in your browser sandbox, without sending your data to any server.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-ink mb-2">
              What formats are supported?
            </h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              Our <strong>free bulk image downloader online</strong> supports all modern image file formats, including PNG, JPG, JPEG, WebP, SVG, AVIF, GIF, and ICO.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Structured FAQ Schema for SEO Rich Snippets -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is this bulk image downloader free to use?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, this is a 100% bulk image downloader free utility. There are no registration forms, no usage limits, and no premium tiers. You can download as many images as you need, whenever you need them."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does it compare to a chrome bulk image downloader extension?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Unlike a bulk image downloader chrome extension, our tool is web-based and does not require installation. This keeps your browser clean and safe from extensions that scan your web history."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I run a bulk image downloader from url list offline?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "While you need an active internet connection to retrieve external images, all image parsing and ZIP packaging tasks are performed locally in your browser sandbox, without sending your data to any server."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What formats are supported?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our free bulk image downloader online supports all modern image file formats, including PNG, JPG, JPEG, WebP, SVG, AVIF, GIF, and ICO."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
